				<r3d:description language="eng">The Progenetix database provides an overview of copy number abnormalities in human cancer from currently 32548 array and chromosomal Comparative Genomic Hybridization (CGH) experiments, as well as Whole Genome or Whole Exome Sequencing (WGS, WES) studies. The cancer profile data in Progenetix was curated from 1031 articles  and represents 366 different cancer types, according to the International classification of Diseases in Oncology (ICD-O).</r3d:description>
